{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "title": "Historical Rocoto production build task graph",
  "authority": "Historical implementation inventory retained from the earlier kit. Paths, policies and statuses below describe that snapshot. Current subject contracts are indexed in docs/INDEX.md; the kit-to-product plan and GitHub issues govern current work. Reconcile individual tasks with those contracts before reuse.",
  "statusValues": [
    "SPECIFIED",
    "KIT",
    "WIRED",
    "PRODUCTION"
  ],
  "statusDefinitions": {
    "SPECIFIED": "Contracted work with no claim that a production connection exists.",
    "KIT": "A design-kit interaction or presentation has been checked; it is not a tenant-safe runtime implementation.",
    "WIRED": "An implemented runtime boundary has named contract evidence in a controlled environment.",
    "PRODUCTION": "A release-gated runtime boundary has live operational evidence; this status never authorizes a deployment by itself."
  },
  "policies": [
    "Stages express dependency order only. They do not shrink scope, grant production authority, or mark an earlier stage as a separate product.",
    "Every command is server-authorized, tenant-scoped, idempotent where retryable, revision-checked where mutable, and auditable.",
    "A client-side flag, a successful-looking control, or a queued job is never proof of an accepted command, external receipt, or completed provider action.",
    "Interaction patterns are local to their surface. There is no global limit on actions or menus; every action must instead have a named owner, state model, accessible name, and evidence path.",
    "Unknown, pending, unavailable, failed, denied, and empty are distinct states. Copy must name the known fact without inventing business data or provider completion.",
    "The graph covers the full production system. An unmet external dependency is a visible blocked condition with a recovery path, not an omitted task or a fabricated success state. A release profile distinguishes capability that is designed, enabled for a tenant, and proven by independent runtime evidence; a built screen or configured connector is neither an enabled capability nor proof of a completed external action.",
    "The `order-review` launch profile enables literal tenant SKU review, reviewed exact-SKU art, explicit accepted uncoded sale-item records, inbound source review, explicit line resolution, reasoned reply attention, unvalued albarans, native provider handoff and print/file output. An uncoded sale item is only admitted from an explicitly accepted off-SKU Albarán line; it retains literal wording/unit and cannot silently become SKU/ERP/stock/tariff master data. Direct related-item links may join coded or uncoded records, are sparse/reciprocal/non-transitive, and never follow category/repetition. Pricing/tariffs, stock/inventory/lots/supplier intake, customer outbound and ERP automation remain designed production leaves, visibly disabled until their own evidence gates pass. Navbar Export, Sales-day and Albarán output doors share one gallery-template → configured-saved-copy → immutable-output-attempt contract. A scheduled subcontractor order-list email, if enabled, is a first-class Export destination with its own recipient rule, attachment/template, schedule, history and truthful provider-receipt contract; it is never customer messaging. WhatsApp starts forward-only at accepted connection time and never exposes earlier history. Only the explicit public-document allowlist may be rendered. Historical operating notes, source conversations, credentials, host details, and fixture content remain outside publication.",
    "Raw inbound email bodies and incoming file bytes are transient only in Rocoto. Original custody stays with the provider/user. Rocoto persists authorized source references, minimal reviewed business facts and actor/parser lineage; it cannot reconstruct a missing original from a summary. THE-SOURCE-PRIVACY-SPEC governs fetch, cache, logging, model input, deletion and legacy cleanup.",
    "E188 closes the English-kit physical UI grammar: inset one-destination rows, unvalued order projections, exact quantity/unit lines, one draft-and-apply filter apparatus, and phone keyboard/thumb navigation. No E188 UI/UX item is deferred. The separately ordered next architecture phase is Runtime/model-to-smartify-runtime/UI-embedded intelligence/Copilot execution; this does not remove or authorize any production leaf."
  ],
